Added two opt-in `PLUGINS_CONFIG` settings for MCP tool discovery, both defaulting to the behaviour an existing deployment already has.
Added `new_tools_enabled`, default `True`. Set it to `False` and a newly discovered tool arrives with `enabled` cleared, so a server that advertises forty tools does not put forty tools on offer before a person has read one of them. `writable` and `enabled` answer different questions: `writable` says a tool needs review before each call, `enabled` says the tool is on offer at all.
Added `disable_on_definition_change`, default `False`. Set it to `True` and discovery clears `enabled` on a tool whose definition fingerprint moved under a review somebody already did. The tool keeps its row, its schemas and its review history, and one click puts it back. The job log names such a tool separately from one that merely changed.
